+This directory contains the `jt` CLI. It uses Spectre.Console.Cli for argument
+binding, help text, validation, and command dispatch.

 ## Build / install locally

 ```bash
 dotnet build src/JobTrack.Cli
 dotnet pack  src/JobTrack.Cli -c Release
 dotnet tool install --global --add-source ./src/JobTrack.Cli/bin/Release JobTrack.Cli
 ```

 Or run without installing:

 ```bash
 dotnet run --project src/JobTrack.Cli -- whoami
 ```

 ## Authentication

 The CLI reads two environment variables:

 | Variable          | Purpose                                                 |
 |-------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
 | `JOBTRACK_API_URL`| Base URL of the JobTrack API. e.g. `http://localhost:5000` |
 | `JOBTRACK_API_KEY`| Service-account API key (form: `jt_<32-byte-base64>`)   |

 Service accounts and keys are created via the JobTrack API
 (`POST /api/service-accounts`) or by an admin in the JobTrack UI.

 The key is sent as `Authorization: Bearer {key}`. The API also accepts
 `X-API-Key: {key}` — either works.

